WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:04.467
-Our first guest is a two-time
Super Bowl champion

00:00:04.467 --> 00:00:06.300
and a Hall of Fame quarterback.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:10.601
He's also the host and producer
of "Manningcast" on ESPN2.

00:00:10.601 --> 00:00:13.834
Ladies and gentlemen, please
welcome Peyton Manning!

00:00:13.834 --> 00:00:15.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:17.400
Peyton, good to see you, bud!

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:20.667
That's what I'm talking about!
-Hey, Jimmy.

00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:23.167
-Peyton, it's great to see you.

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:24.534
Welcome back.

00:00:24.534 --> 00:00:27.267
You had a great cameo
on "Saturday Night Live"

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:29.234
during "Weekend Update"
this past week.

00:00:29.234 --> 00:00:31.000
I loved it.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.834
Colin Jost wanted to have you on
to talk about football,

00:00:33.834 --> 00:00:37.834
and all you wanted to talk about
was "Emily in Paris."

00:00:37.834 --> 00:00:39.734
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.734 --> 00:00:41.467
I want to know,
have you ever seen

00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:43.868
an episode of "Emily in Paris"?

00:00:43.868 --> 00:00:47.434
-I've never seen an episode of
"Emily in Paris."

00:00:47.434 --> 00:00:50.400
Not sure if I'm going to
in the future.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:53.033
I feel like I know so much about
it now, Jimmy.

00:00:53.033 --> 00:00:55.234
But I think I'm going to be
asked to be

00:00:55.234 --> 00:00:57.133
in season three,
like a big part.

00:00:57.133 --> 00:00:58.234
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.234 --> 00:01:01.434
-It was well done. It's so good.

00:01:01.434 --> 00:01:03.934
I have to ask you because
everyone is talking about this.

00:01:03.934 --> 00:01:05.400
And I thought it was insane

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.767
kind of because I'm watching
the games this weekend.

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:11.801
And they go, "Ugh, we have to
announce Tom Brady is retiring."

00:01:11.801 --> 00:01:14.701
And then they do a whole
documentary, slow motion of

00:01:14.701 --> 00:01:16.834
him walking out on the field,
and they go,

00:01:16.834 --> 00:01:19.667
"And also, he hasn't really
decided if he's retiring."

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:21.300
[ Laughter ]
"Okay, I'm sorry."

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:23.701
We just watched a whole
documentary of how great he was.

00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:25.567
What's your lead on this?

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:27.834
Is he retiring? Is he not?

00:01:27.834 --> 00:01:29.868
-Yeah, I'm not sure
I have the answer.

00:01:29.868 --> 00:01:32.200
But I think
if Tom's going to retire,

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:34.634
I feel like he'll announce it
himself.

00:01:34.634 --> 00:01:38.267
That's kind of the process that
I went through when I retired.

00:01:38.267 --> 00:01:41.901
Jimmy in 2011 when I got injured
with the Colts,

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.467
there were a lot of rumors
whether I was going to

00:01:43.467 --> 00:01:45.033
come back and play or not.

00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:48.601
Rob Lowe tweeted out
that he knew firsthand

00:01:48.601 --> 00:01:50.601
that I was about to retire.

00:01:50.601 --> 00:01:54.734
And I had to call a press
conference to actually say,

00:01:54.734 --> 00:01:58.067
"You know, I always thought I
would announce my retirement,

00:01:58.067 --> 00:02:01.334
not the guy that played Sodapop
Curtis in 'The Outsiders.'"

00:02:01.334 --> 00:02:04.801
[ Laughter ]
-You'd think.

00:02:04.801 --> 00:02:07.868
-I feel like Tom is
in that same boat a little bit.

00:02:07.868 --> 00:02:10.033
Like, I think he'll make
the announcement

00:02:10.033 --> 00:02:11.534
at the appropriate time.

00:02:11.534 --> 00:02:14.000
It might be tomorrow.
It might be in April.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.000
It might not be till three years
from now, he's playing so well.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:20.634
So I don't imagine
Tom's too happy

00:02:20.634 --> 00:02:22.567
with the news this weekend.

00:02:22.567 --> 00:02:25.234
But I think he will announce it
whenever,

00:02:25.234 --> 00:02:28.634
at the appropriate time,
on his own terms, as he should.

00:02:28.634 --> 00:02:30.734
-Yeah, I agree. Good man.

00:02:30.734 --> 00:02:32.834
Peyton, you're one of
the greatest quarterbacks

00:02:32.834 --> 00:02:34.801
to ever play the game.

00:02:34.801 --> 00:02:38.801
And then I saw you throw out
a first pitch

00:02:38.801 --> 00:02:40.767
at an all-star game.

00:02:40.767 --> 00:02:43.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.133 --> 00:02:44.701
Should we show the clip?

00:02:44.701 --> 00:02:47.033
-No. No clip, please. No clip.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.200
Please.
[ Drumroll ]

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.200
-I'm sorry. Don't look.
Cover your eyes.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:51.534
Cover your eyes for one second.

00:02:51.534 --> 00:02:52.901
Let's just take a look
real quick.

00:02:52.901 --> 00:02:54.734
Here's Peyton Manning throwing
out the first pitch here.

00:02:59.868 --> 00:03:03.634
-Alright, now,
now, it's very hard.

00:03:03.634 --> 00:03:06.467
I've done it myself and failed.

00:03:06.467 --> 00:03:09.100
It's harder than you think.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:11.434
-Yeah.
It was bad all the way around.

00:03:11.434 --> 00:03:13.133
First off, they were
supposed to have

00:03:13.133 --> 00:03:16.334
two Colorado Rockies players
do it.

00:03:16.334 --> 00:03:19.501
One got COVID.
The other had knee surgery.

00:03:19.501 --> 00:03:22.000
So, they bring in the
third-string quarterback, right?

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:25.234
The third stringer should not be
throwing out the first pitch

00:03:25.234 --> 00:03:27.934
at an all-star game, Jimmy.
-You're the third-stringer here.

00:03:27.934 --> 00:03:30.033
-Yeah.
I wasn't mentally prepared.

00:03:30.033 --> 00:03:33.267
I had one-day notice.
I didn't get a lot of practice.

00:03:33.267 --> 00:03:34.834
And I got too much coaching.

00:03:34.834 --> 00:03:37.701
Max Scherzer told me
to throw it hard.

00:03:37.701 --> 00:03:40.701
Ohtani told me just get it
over the plate.

00:03:40.701 --> 00:03:42.701
I couldn't make my mind up.
I'm winding up.

00:03:42.701 --> 00:03:44.300
I'm like, "Throw it hard,
throw it hard.

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:46.434
No, no, throw it soft."
And I'm in between.

00:03:46.434 --> 00:03:48.834
And I threw an interception
right in the dirt.

00:03:48.834 --> 00:03:50.200
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.567
I mean, what's
the statute of limitations

00:03:52.567 --> 00:03:55.067
on when that video
stops being played?

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:57.701
Eli I feel like is
behind this episode

00:03:57.701 --> 00:03:59.267
and making you show that video.

00:03:59.267 --> 00:04:00.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:03.367
-Eli had a little bit
to do with it.

00:04:03.367 --> 00:04:06.667
I remember the first time
I met you and your brother,

00:04:06.667 --> 00:04:09.200
we were in Indianapolis at --
Oh, no.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:10.968
We were in Kentucky
at the Kentucky Derby.

00:04:10.968 --> 00:04:12.734
-Kentucky. Kentucky Derby.

00:04:12.734 --> 00:04:16.000
-And the Colts were there
and you were there with Eli.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:18.400
And I jumped on stage to sing
with the band

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:21.801
or something like that and I was
dating my now-wife at the time.

00:04:21.801 --> 00:04:23.934
And it came down and all
the Colts were there,

00:04:23.934 --> 00:04:27.968
and I go, "Where's Nancy?
Where's my girlfriend?"

00:04:27.968 --> 00:04:29.767
They go, "She's the best, man.

00:04:29.767 --> 00:04:31.634
She's so cool."
I go, "I know. Where is she?"

00:04:31.634 --> 00:04:33.467
They go, "She's partying with
the Mannings."

00:04:33.467 --> 00:04:37.133
And she was next to you and she
was chugging a bottle of vodka.

00:04:37.133 --> 00:04:39.701
And I was like, "You don't do
that. What are you doing?"

00:04:39.701 --> 00:04:41.734
She was like,
"These guys are so fun."

00:04:41.734 --> 00:04:43.834
-My Colts teammates loved her.

00:04:43.834 --> 00:04:47.400
They wanted her to draft her to
come back to play for our team.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:48.834
She is one of us.

00:04:48.834 --> 00:04:49.901
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.901 --> 00:04:51.601
-The Manning brothers.
It was so fun.

00:04:51.601 --> 00:04:54.000
We had the best time.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.701
"Manningcast" can't be funnier,
can't be better,

00:04:56.701 --> 00:04:58.701
so well-produced, well-done.

00:04:58.701 --> 00:05:01.634
It's you and your brother
making fun of each other.

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:04.534
But also you're geniuses
about football.

00:05:04.534 --> 00:05:06.834
-Yeah. I mean Jimmy, it's just
something different.

00:05:06.834 --> 00:05:09.467
We were real happy
that ESPN kind of wanted

00:05:09.467 --> 00:05:11.033
to do something different.

00:05:11.033 --> 00:05:12.634
Eli and I thought
they were joking.

00:05:12.634 --> 00:05:16.501
"Wait a minute, you're going to
pay us to watch football

00:05:16.501 --> 00:05:18.434
with my brother from our house?"

00:05:18.434 --> 00:05:21.100
[ Laughter ]
Like, I know I went to Tennessee

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:23.501
and Eli went to Ole Miss,
but I think we can figure out

00:05:23.501 --> 00:05:26.334
this sounds like a lot of fun
and a pretty good deal.

00:05:26.334 --> 00:05:29.267
We get to be home
on the weekends with our kids

00:05:29.267 --> 00:05:32.334
and coach their sports and still
stay close to the game of

00:05:32.334 --> 00:05:34.667
football, talking about it
in a fun way.

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:36.968
We had some great guests
on this year,

00:05:36.968 --> 00:05:38.734
all people that love football.

00:05:38.734 --> 00:05:40.801
But it's a lot of fun to do it
with my brother, Jimmy.

00:05:40.801 --> 00:05:42.634
You know, he's in New York,
I'm in Denver.

00:05:42.634 --> 00:05:45.200
We don't see each other as much
as we used to.

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:48.067
So for he and I have to have
this together every Monday

00:05:48.067 --> 00:05:51.334
or 10 Mondays in the fall,
it's been a lot of fun.

00:05:51.334 --> 00:05:54.434
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Alright. Quickly, Super Bowl.

00:05:54.434 --> 00:05:56.501
Now it's down to
Bengals versus Rams.

00:05:56.501 --> 00:05:58.701
I don't know if anyone saw
this coming.

00:05:58.701 --> 00:06:01.834
I didn't. But I have no idea
who's going to win.

00:06:01.834 --> 00:06:04.868
I don't even know who has
the advantage or disadvantage.

00:06:04.868 --> 00:06:07.968
-Well, obviously the puppy race
tells it all.

00:06:07.968 --> 00:06:10.400
It's definitely going to be
Bengals, right?

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:12.434
-Ron beat Gary.

00:06:12.434 --> 00:06:15.501
Look, I'm so pumped for
these quarterbacks, right?

00:06:15.501 --> 00:06:18.000
Matthew Stafford, 13 years,
right?

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:20.067
You know, he's been taking
a lot of heat.

00:06:20.067 --> 00:06:21.667
Can he win the big one,
all that?

00:06:21.667 --> 00:06:23.367
I'm so glad he's there.

00:06:23.367 --> 00:06:25.501
And Joe Burrow is just Mr. Cool,
right?

00:06:25.501 --> 00:06:27.300
I mean, to be in a Super Bowl --

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:30.067
in his first Super Bowl
so early in his career.

00:06:30.067 --> 00:06:32.167
Both these guys
will handle the moment.

00:06:32.167 --> 00:06:34.801
You know, obviously one of them
is going to come away a winner.

00:06:34.801 --> 00:06:36.234
I've been on both sides of it.

00:06:36.234 --> 00:06:38.200
There's no feeling
like to win it, Jimmy.

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:41.133
It is as disappointing as you
think it would be not to win it.

00:06:41.133 --> 00:06:43.367
So I'm pulling for
both quarterbacks.

00:06:43.367 --> 00:06:45.334
It's going to be a great game
without a doubt.

00:06:45.334 --> 00:06:48.501
-A legend right there.
Peyton Manning, everybody.

00:06:48.501 --> 00:06:51.300
Check out his commercial also
during the big game.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:52.868
You're doing Michelob?

00:06:52.868 --> 00:06:54.067
-Michelob Ultra.
Just like you did, man.

00:06:54.067 --> 00:06:57.234
-Michelob Ultra, baby!
That's my jam! I love it!

00:06:57.234 --> 00:06:58.801
Check out his commercial
during the big game.

00:06:58.801 --> 00:06:59.801
We love you, pal.

